Node.js is an external runtime, not bundled. OpenAPI is a specification reference.
No third-party API testing framework implementation was copied.
Schemathesis is referenced for a documented capability comparison only.
The optional Node standards adapter uses pinned Swagger Parser (MIT),
Ajv Draft-04 and ajv-formats (MIT), OpenAPI Enforcer (Apache-2.0), and
yaml (ISC), with transitive dependencies listed in docs/THIRD_PARTY.md.
The standards adapter also uses lossless-json 4.3.3 (MIT) and saxes 6.0.0
(ISC), with xmlchars 2.2.0 (MIT). The pinned JSON Schema Test Suite vectors
retain their upstream MIT notice in tests/vectors/LICENSE.
They are installed separately with npm ci; their upstream notices/licenses
remain in those packages. The dependency-free legacy runtime bundle does not
include these libraries or the new standards entry point.
The separate standards runtime bundle installs these exact locked dependencies
and retains their original license/notice files inside node_modules.
Schemathesis is executed only as an optional, separately installed reference
tool in an isolated comparison environment; it is not redistributed.
The optional integration script starts a separately obtained PocketBase 0.40.5
binary (MIT, Copyright 2022-present Gani Georgiev); it is not redistributed.
Test collection migrations and adapter contracts are original MoonAPI fixtures.
